{
  "headline": "President Mahama inspects poultry processing plant construction in Bechem, Ghana",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "President John Dramani Mahama inspected ongoing construction of the Poultry, Meat and Feed Processing Plant in Bechem, located in the Ahafo Region of Ghana. The inspection was conducted as part of the first day of the President's two-day Resetting Ghana tour of the Ahafo Region. During the visit, Mahama stated that once the factory is operational, it is projected to position Bechem as the chicken capital of Ghana and create jobs for more people. He advised local youth to enter the poultry farming industry to utilize the factory's market. The President noted that the Nkokɔ Nketenkete initiative was started to ensure a value chain for the poultry industry prior to the commencement of factory work. Mahama, who cut the sod for the project on November 27, 2025, expressed satisfaction with the progress, reporting that work has reached approximately 50 per cent completion. He commended the project's consultants, Architecture and Engineering Services Limited (AESL), for their work. The facility is expected to be ready for commissioning by the end of the first quarter of 2027. Separately, the Minister of Food and Agriculture, Eric Opoku, stated that following the launch of the Nkokɔ Nketenkete initiative under the Feed Ghana Programme, Ghana's domestic poultry production increased from 4.6 per cent to 22 per cent as of May 2026."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "headline": "Winners of BRAC Bank-Samakal Literary Awards 2024-2025 announced in Dhaka, Bangladesh",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "The winners of the BRAC Bank-Samakal Literary Awards for 2024 and 2025 were announced at a ceremony held at the Pan Pacific Sonargaon Hotel in Dhaka on October 9, 2026, according to a press release. The awards, organized by BRAC Bank and Daily Samakal, aim to promote Bangla literature and inspire writers. The ceremony featured Chief Guest Dr. Wahiduddin Mahmud, an eminent economist and adviser to the caretaker government, alongside various media and banking executives and literary figures. The Lifetime Achievement Award, which includes a Tk. 5 lakh prize, was presented to writer Prof Serajul Islam Choudhury for 2024 and novelist Selina Hossain for 2025. Other prize categories included the essay, autobiography, travel, and translation category (Tk. 3 lakh), the poetry and novel category (Tk. 3 lakh), and the Young Writer Award (Tk. 2 lakh). All winners also received a crest and citation."
    },
    {
      "text": "For the 2024 BRAC Bank–Daily Samakal Literary Award, Abul Ahsan Choudhury won in the essay, autobiography, travel, and translation category for the book “Vidyasagar, Bankimchandra, Rabindranath and Musolman Samaj.” Anwara Syed Haq won in the poetry and novel category for “Shomoy Bohiya Gelo,” and Nizam Biswas received the Young Writer Award for “Jolmakorer Noukabaich.” For the 2025 awards, Nasreen Jahan won in the essay, autobiography, travel, and translation category for “Paloker Chinhogulo,” Shaheen Akhtar won in the poetry and novel category for “Manchitra,” and Mahbub Mayukh Rishad received the Young Writer Award for “Cyanide Phool.”"
    }
  ]
}

